#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:1
msgid "Change Log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:3
msgid "0.8.0 - 2026-11-10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:5
msgid ""
"New components (accordion, aside, steps, vertical tab sets, and explicit "
"card header and footer directives), links that open in a new tab, badge "
"tooltips, a plain-CSS build with no Sass, tab selections that persist across "
"pages and visits, accessibility fixes, FontAwesome v6 support, and Octicons "
"v19.42.0. Sphinx 7.2 or later is now required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:10
msgid "Upgrade notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:12
msgid ""
"**Sphinx `>=7.2` is required** (Sphinx 7.0 and 7.1 are no longer supported); "
"Python stays at `>=3.11` ({pr}`276`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:13
msgid ""
"**The `^^^` and `+++` card separators are deprecated and warn by default.** "
"They still render as before, but the first card in a document that uses them "
"emits one `design.card_legacy` warning, so a build run with `-W` fails until "
"you do one of two things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:16
msgid ""
"move the header and footer into the new `card-header` and `card-footer` "
"directives (or the one-line `:header:` and `:footer:` options), which need "
"sphinx-design 0.8.0 or later; or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:18
msgid "add `\"design.card_legacy\"` to `suppress_warnings` in your `conf.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:20
msgid ""
"Once every card is migrated, set `sd_card_legacy_separators = False` to stop "
"scanning for the separators. The plan is to turn the separators off by "
"default in 1.0 and remove them in 2.0; the cards page has a migration table "
"({pr}`294`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:23
msgid ""
"**Tab selections persist in `localStorage`** instead of `sessionStorage`, so "
"a chosen tab is remembered across browsing sessions as well as across pages. "
"The storage key prefix is set by the new `sd_tabs_storage_prefix` option; "
"set it to an empty string to disable persistence ({pr}`284`, {issue}`103`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:27
msgid ""
"**Static assets are served through Sphinx's `html_static_path`**, only for "
"HTML-format builders. A `_sphinx_design_static` directory left in an "
"existing build directory by an earlier version is unused and can be deleted "
"({pr}`276`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:30
msgid ""
"**The stylesheet is plain CSS**, generated without Sass. The `--sd-color-*-"
"highlight` hover and focus shades are now derived at runtime with `color-"
"mix()` (behind the old value as a static fallback), so overriding a `--sd-"
"color-*` variable now also changes its hover shade ({pr}`290`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:33
msgid ""
"**The private `sphinx_design._compat.findall` helper is removed**; call "
"`node.findall(...)` directly ({pr}`276`). The private "
"`CardDirective._create_component` method is renamed `_create_slot`; the old "
"name stays as an alias for one release ({pr}`294`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:36
msgid ""
"**`sd-card-text` is added only to the direct child paragraphs** of a card or "
"dropdown body, and is added to a paragraph's classes instead of replacing "
"them; paragraphs nested deeper (in admonitions, lists, nested tab sets) no "
"longer get it ({pr}`278`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:40 ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:176
msgid "New"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:42
msgid ""
"✨ `accordion` directive: groups `dropdown`s so that opening one closes the "
"others, using the browser's native `<details name>` behaviour with no "
"JavaScript; `:flush:` renders it edge to edge by {user}`chrisjsewell` in {pr}"
"`291`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:45
msgid ""
"✨ `aside` directive: a call-out box floated beside the body text "
"(`:align:`, `:width:`), rendered as a semantic `<aside>` in HTML and a plain "
"titled container elsewhere by {user}`chrisjsewell` in {pr}`292` ({issue}`97`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:48
msgid ""
"✨ `steps` and `step` directives for numbered procedures, with CSS-only "
"number markers on an ordered list, `:start:` and `:color:` options by {user}"
"`chrisjsewell` in {pr}`293`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:50
msgid ""
"✨ `card-header` and `card-footer` directives, and `:header:` and `:footer:` "
"options, for card and grid-item-card headers and footers: the card body is "
"parsed once as ordinary content, and errors in a header or footer report "
"their own line (see the upgrade notes for the legacy separators) by {user}"
"`chrisjsewell` in {pr}`294`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:54
msgid ""
"✨ Vertical tab sets: `tab-set` and `tab-set-code` take `:orientation: "
"vertical`, which stacks the labels in a rail beside the selected panel from "
"the `md` breakpoint up by {user}`kdeldycke` in {pr}`304` ({issue}`219`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:57
msgid ""
"✨ Open links in a new tab: the `link-new-tab` flag on `card` and `grid-item-"
"card`, and `new-tab` on `button-link` and `button-ref`, for URLs and "
"internal references alike by {user}`dipinknair` in {pr}`298` ({issue}`170`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:60
msgid ""
"✨ Badge tooltips: badge roles accept a trailing `` ; tooltip `` suffix, "
"rendered as a native HTML `title`; for link and ref badges it applies after "
"the explicit `text <target>` form, and `` \\; `` escapes a literal semicolon "
"by {user}`chrisjsewell` in {pr}`286` ({issue}`81`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:63
msgid ""
"✨ Every badge role (plain, line, link and ref, in every colour) accepts a "
"`tooltip` role option, so a reStructuredText custom role (`.. role:: bdg-"
"stable(bdg-success)` with `:tooltip:`) or an extension can preset a tooltip; "
"a `; tooltip` suffix still takes precedence by {user}`chrisjsewell` in {pr}"
"`316`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:67
msgid ""
"✨ A line block in `button-link` or `button-ref` text renders as separate "
"lines (`<br />` in HTML, `\\newline{}` in LaTeX), each line its own gettext "
"message by {user}`Cherith1222` in {pr}`308` and {user}`chrisjsewell` in {pr}"
"`315` ({issue}`156`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:70
msgid ""
"✨ A URL fragment that targets a tab (e.g. `page.html#tab-name`), or an "
"element inside a tab panel, opens that tab, on load and on `hashchange` by "
"{user}`chrisjsewell` in {pr}`284` ({issue}`239`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:72
msgid ""
"✨ FontAwesome v6 roles (`fa-solid`, `fa-brands`, `fa-regular`), and CSS "
"loading via the new `sd_fontawesome_source` and `sd_fontawesome_cdn_url` "
"options (the supported path for FontAwesome Pro kits) by {user}"
"`chrisjsewell` in {pr}`285` ({issue}`174`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:75
msgid ""
"✨ `sd_fontawesome_version` makes icon role names version-agnostic: any "
"spelling (`fas`, `fa-solid`, ...) can emit the FontAwesome `\"4\"`, `\"5\"` "
"or `\"6\"` class scheme, so upgrading FontAwesome is a one-line `conf.py` "
"change; the default `\"as-named\"` keeps emitting the role name as before by "
"{user}`chrisjsewell` in {pr}`288` ({issue}`174`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:78
msgid ""
"✨ `sphinx_design.testing` module with the `normalize_doctree_xml` helper, "
"for downstream extensions' doctree regression tests by {user}`chrisjsewell` "
"in {pr}`277` ({issue}`260`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:81 ../../../../CHANGELOG.md:221
msgid "Improve"
msgstr ""

